  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CONSERVING THE NGORONGORO BLACK RHINO POPULATION IN NORTHERN TANZANIA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to support a conservation effort in Ngorongoro, Tanzania by studying and monitoring the black rhinoceros population to meet growth targets based on rigorous scientific data for long-term viability. This project is intended to conserve the Eastern black rhinoceros and their habitat by addressing the lack of metapopulation analysis and management in a changing landscape. Specific activities include: (1) designing a long-term monitoring program; and (2) analyzing habitat use and diet to assess the ecological carrying capacity in Ngorongoro Conservation Area for the improvement of black rhinoceros monitoring and management for the future.</narrative>
  </description>
